  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA-only multiprofile PCA with avgpool is the best configuration (accuracy 0.591, F1 0.573), clearly outperforming single-profile RNA and transformer aggregation, while image-only ResNet50 is weak (accuracy 0.208). The key uncertainty is whether image features can complement the strong RNA baseline in a multimodal model. config_018 tests this by adding ResNet50 image features to the best known RNA setup while keeping profile setting, RNA encoder, and aggregation fixed, using simple concat fusion as a baseline. This is the best next experiment because it directly extends the strongest evidence, isolates the contribution of adding image information as much as possible, and will clarify whether multimodal fusion is worth further investment under the limited budget."
}

